 "tier": "core",
 "title": "Lloyd's Mirror",
 "oneLine": "A slit and its reflection in a grazing mirror interfere; the fringes are like Young's with d = 2h, but the centre is dark.",
 "statement": "A slit $S$ at height $h$ above a plane mirror and its virtual image $S^{\\prime}$ (depth $h$ below) act as a pair of coherent sources $d=2h$ apart; a screen at distance $D$ gives\n$$\\beta=\\frac{\\lambda D}{2h}.$$\nAt the mirror edge (zero geometric path difference) the fringe is <b>dark</b>: the reflected beam undergoes a phase change of $\\pi$.",
